ssage. Prove it by diffing the failure names AND messages, record the proof on this task, then `gh pr merge --squash --admin`. Anything else red: fix it if it's in the PR's own change, otherwise stop and report.\n- After each merge, fetch and run the FOCUSED suites for what merged (execution spawn/context tests; prompt tests; server spawn-selection pg + headers). Run typecheck and the build on the merged main. A green PR can still red the merged tree, especially stacked or colliding PRs.\n- Before running tests, run `uptime`. If the load is above ~80, wait. Heavy parallel lanes fake failures.\n- Link each merged PR to its task with `tm8 task link-pr` if it isn't linked. Mark I6 (01a0d3b2-28c9), F3 (01a0d3b2-474a) and I5 (01a0d3b2-22ce) done once all their parts have merged.\n- Never force-push a branch you don't own without rebasing ON TOP of its current head. Never `git branch -D` by pattern. Never `git stash`.\n\nCoordination: FIRST, post on coordinator task 01a0d3b0-339e-7d9b-ab82-4c87139fa22d and on the owner tasks A (01a0d45a-9ff5), B (01a0d45a-a201) and C (01a0d45a-a315) that you are now the merger for this queue at Subhang's request, so nobody double-merges. If an owner replies that a merge is already in flight, let theirs finish.\nPost a milestone message on THIS task after each merge (PR, merge sha, suites run). Deploy notes doc 01a0d454-9e01-74f2-a115-71c97b0424b0: update it with what each merge changes on deploy. From I6 on, deploy the server first, or server and CLI together. You do NOT deploy.\n\nFIRST COMMAND: `git fetch origin && git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main`. If it's not 0, `git merge --ff-only origin/main`. If node_modules is missing, run `bun install`.\n",
